NoriDeck Portal
===============

The public site for the NoriDeck console: a short introduction, how to use
it, how to make cartridges, and where to download the installer. It is a
static site (HTML, CSS, and a little JavaScript) with no server program and
no database. Installers, versions, release notes, and download counts all
come from GitHub Releases of NGHSLab/NoriDeck.


Features
--------

  Home (/)
    Short introduction with a download button for the visitor's platform,
    the latest version line, a usage guide in four steps, the default key
    map, notes on making cartridges (npm create nori, nori build, NoriHub),
    and links to related services.

  Downloads (/download)
    Latest release   : file table per platform (installer, portable, sample
                       cartridge) with sizes and a link to GitHub
    Install guide    : Windows installer and portable steps, system
                       requirements
    Release history  : previous releases with their release notes
                       (/releases redirects to /download#history)

  Release notes
    The Markdown body of each GitHub release is shown the same way GitHub
    renders it (tables, code blocks, links). Release notes are not
    translated.

  Korean and English
    The globe menu in the header switches the language. The choice is
    remembered in the browser; Korean is the default.


How release data is loaded
--------------------------

  The visitor's browser, not a server, reads the release list from the
  GitHub API:

    GET https://api.github.com/repos/NGHSLab/NoriDeck/releases?per_page=20
    Accept: application/vnd.github.full+json   (includes body_html)

  Successful responses are cached in sessionStorage for 10 minutes per tab,
  so moving between pages does not call the API again. When the API fails
  (rate limit, network), the download button falls back to /download and
  the download page links to GitHub Releases directly.

  Release assets are classified by file name (electron-builder defaults;
  GitHub turns spaces into dots):

    NoriDeck.Setup.x.y.z.exe   installer
    NoriDeck.x.y.z.exe         portable (other .exe)
    *.tar.gz (linux)           Linux portable
    *.nori                     sample cartridge
    latest.yml, *.blockmap     hidden (auto-update files)

  GitHub's rendered body_html is sanitized again with DOMPurify before it
  is inserted. Everything else from the API is inserted as text only.

  The NoriDeck repository must be public for any of this to work.


Tech stack
----------

  Static HTML and CSS, plain JavaScript ES modules, no framework, no build
  DOMPurify 3 (vendored in site/assets/vendor)
  nginx 1.24 on Rocky Linux 8 (installed with dnf)
  Node.js 20+ for local preview, tests (node --test), and prettier


Project layout
--------------

  site/                        everything that is deployed (nginx root)
    index.html                 home
    download.html              downloads and release history
    404.html
    assets/css/site.css
    assets/js/lib.js           pure functions (asset classification,
                               platform detection, formatting)
    assets/js/releases.js      GitHub API client and cache
    assets/js/i18n.js          language switching
    assets/js/messages.js      English strings and generated strings
    assets/js/locale-boot.js   applies the saved language before paint
    assets/js/home.js          home page rendering
    assets/js/download.js      download page rendering
    assets/img/                illustrations and favicon
    assets/vendor/             DOMPurify (do not edit)
  tests/                       node --test (lib, i18n key coverage)
  scripts/serve.mjs            local preview server with nginx routing
  scripts/download-stats.mjs   download counts per release
  deploy/                      install.sh, deploy.sh, nginx config
  docs/portal-plan.md          roadmap
  prototype/                   early mockups and the illustration script


Getting started
---------------

  1. Install the dev tools
       npm install
     This installs prettier only. The site itself needs nothing.

  2. Run
       npm run dev
     Opens a preview at http://localhost:8080 with the same routing as
     nginx (/download, /releases, 404).

  3. Verify
       npm run check
     Runs the prettier format check and all tests. CI runs the same
     command on every push.


Publishing a new console version
--------------------------------

  Done in the NoriDeck repository; the portal itself does not change.

  1. Build with npm run build:desktop and attach the files from
     desktop/release/ to a new GitHub Release:
       NoriDeck Setup x.y.z.exe   installer (required)
       NoriDeck x.y.z.exe         portable
       *.nori                     optional sample cartridge
       latest.yml, *.blockmap     optional, for future auto-update
  2. Tag it like v0.1.3 and write the release notes in Markdown.
  3. Publish. The new version shows on the portal on the next visit.

  If installer file names change, update classifyAsset in
  site/assets/js/lib.js and its tests together.


Download counts
---------------

  GitHub keeps a cumulative count per file.

    npm run stats                cumulative counts per release and file
    npm run stats -- --csv       date,version,file,count (collect daily
                                 for trends)

  latest.yml and .blockmap files are excluded from totals. Set
  GITHUB_TOKEN if the API rate limit is hit.


Deployment
----------

  nginx installed with dnf on Rocky Linux 8 serves site/ directly. An L7
  switch in front terminates HTTPS and forwards to the VM on port 8080.
  See deploy/README.md for details.

    First install (root)   L7_IP=<L7 IP> bash deploy/install.sh
    Update (deploy user)   /opt/norideck-portal/deploy/deploy.sh

  install.sh is safe to run again. Run it again whenever deploy/nginx/
  changes; deploy.sh only syncs the files.


